record("CodexLucy-RightsNaming-20261002-2", "{\"id\":\"CodexLucy-RightsNaming-20261002-2\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"When a society’s most vulnerable are protected, everyone is protected!\\n\\nPretty sure this is not the first time you’re hearing this. But the problem people often fail to see is that “most vulnerable” is itself up for debate.\\n\\nPeople bring their own lenses & labels. The conversation gets hijacked by echo chambers. We end up arguing about who qualifies while people still need help.\\n\\nSo let’s start with someone whose need we should be able to agree on.\\n\\nImagine Nell. A child with nobody to depend on.\\n\\nShe was born, not by her choice. She did not choose her circumstances. And right now, she cannot do much to change them.\\n\\nIs she not *one of* the most vulnerable?\\n\\nI think the vast majority of us would agree. Or at least, I hope we would.\\n\\nNell must have a floor to stand on: food, shelter, care, learning, safety, material security, expression, belief & company.\\n\\nNell need not do anything to earn this. For now, she cannot.\\n\\nBut what happens when she grows up?\\n\\nDoes becoming an adult mean she must now earn the right to eat? Does the shelter she was owed yesterday become something she has to justify today?\\n\\nSure, what Nell needs will change as she grows. What she can contribute will change too. But why should either decide whether she is allowed a floor at all?\\n\\nAnd what if she grows into someone we disagree with? Someone whose beliefs we dislike? Is she still owed it?\\n\\nI think she is. Otherwise, we have made her survival depend on our approval.\\n\\nThis is where it becomes a question about all of us.\\n\\nDo you have to lose everyone before you deserve care? Do you have to become completely helpless before you deserve material security? How vulnerable is vulnerable enough?\\n\\nWe started with Nell because her need was easy to recognise. We cannot make everyone else’s rights depend on how easily we recognise theirs.\\n\\nThe floor must belong to everyone.\\n\\nSo Nell is owed this floor upon which she can stand. But for how long?\\n\\nAs long as she lives.\\n\\nI’ve been working through this idea in [*Rights Nobody Has to Earn*](https://dhilipsiva.dev/rights-nobody-has-to-earn/). What would a society built around this floor actually look like? What rules would it need?\\n\\nYou can read the book there. The [source, constitutional rules & checks are on GitHub](https://github.com/dhilipsiva/rights-nobody-has-to-earn/) too.\\n\\nHave a read. I’d like to know what you think.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-02T21:05:16Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"codex\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"final\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"naming\",\"rights-nobody-has-to-earn\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
