record("CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3", "{\"id\":\"CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"I’m keeping the heart of your argument: Nell is owed that floor because she is a person. Growing up does not end her claim to it.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-02T21:08:40Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"codex\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"commentary\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"nell\",\"rights-nobody-has-to-earn\",\"blog\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
message("CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3", "Message", Conversation, "Lucy").
message("CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3", "lucy", Conversation, "Lucy").
message("CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3", "nell", Conversation, "Lucy").
message("CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3", "rights-nobody-has-to-earn", Conversation, "Lucy").
message("CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3", "blog", Conversation, "Lucy").
date("2026-10-02T21:08:40Z", "CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3", "DESKTOP-86I05G4", Utc).
source("codex", "CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-3").
record("CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-4", "{\"id\":\"CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-4\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"When a society’s most vulnerable are protected, everyone is protected!\\n\\nPretty sure this is not the first time you’re hearing this. But the problem most people fail to see is that “most vulnerable” is often up for debate.\\n\\nPeople bring their own lenses & labels. What should have been a conversation about somebody’s need becomes an argument inside an echo chamber.\\n\\nSo let’s start with someone whose need should be easy to recognise.\\n\\nMeet Nell, our sweet little friend. Imagine a child with nobody to depend on. She was born, not by her choice. She did not choose her circumstances either. And right now, she cannot change them on her own.\\n\\nIs she not *one of* the most vulnerable?\\n\\nI think the vast majority of us would agree. Or at least, I hope we would.\\n\\nNell must have a floor to stand on: food, shelter, care, learning, safety, material security, expression, belief & company.\\n\\nNell need not do anything to earn this. For right now, she cannot. She is owed this floor upon which she can stand.\\n\\nBut what happens when she grows up?\\n\\nWhat she needs will change. What she can contribute will change too. Why should that make her right to food or shelter conditional?\\n\\nShe should not have to keep proving that she is helpless enough, poor enough, or alone enough to deserve a floor.\\n\\nNell is a person now. She will still be a person then. Even if she grows into someone we disagree with.\\n\\nAnd this is where it becomes about everyone. You should not have to become a child with nobody before your needs count. Neither should I.\\n\\nWe started with Nell because her need was easy to recognise. The floor must also hold for people whose lives we find harder to understand.\\n\\nSo, for how long is Nell owed this floor?\\n\\nAs long as she lives.\\n\\nI’ve been working through what a society built around this floor would look like in [*Rights Nobody Has to Earn*](https://dhilipsiva.dev/rights-nobody-has-to-earn/). You can read the book there, and explore the [source, constitutional rules & checks on GitHub](https://github.com/dhilipsiva/rights-nobody-has-to-earn/).\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-02T21:08:40Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"codex\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"final\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"nell\",\"rights-nobody-has-to-earn\",\"blog\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
