record("CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-15", "{\"id\":\"CodexLucy-NellBlog-20261002-15\",\"speaker\":\"Dhilipsiva\",\"text\":\"And people also suffer a mass-delution: \\\"If everybody is given everything, then why would anybody do anything? They will become lazy!\\\". Honestly this can be disarmed with a simple mental math. Think of all the people you every know. How many of them would not not like to get paid a little bit more? So that, they could offord better phones, better homes, better cars, those expensive dining at that restauraty they like. And that requires money. I mean who does not like a option to have a better life, even if it would only make marginally better, most people would pursue it. Seems like a no-brainer\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-02T21:29:59Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"codex\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"user\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"nell\",\"blog\",\"incentives\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
